    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Apache XTable™ (Incubating) 0.5.0 Release]]></title>
        <id>https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release</id>
        <link href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release"/>
        <updated>2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
        <summary type="html"><![CDATA[Apache XTable™ (Incubating) 0.5.0 moves to Apache Hudi 1.2.1, adds a Hudi-backed secondary index for any source table, and fixes the license issues left open in 0.4.0.]]></summary>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>We are pleased to announce the release of 0.5.0-incubating, which lands 79 commits from
15 contributors.
See the <a class="" href="https://xtable.apache.org/releases/release-0.5.0-incubating">release notes</a> for the complete list of changes.</p>
<p>Apache XTable™ (Incubating) converts metadata between Apache Hudi, Apache Iceberg and Delta Lake
without rewriting any data files. It also supports Apache Paimon and Apache Parquet tables as
sources.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="release-highlights">Release Highlights<a href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release#release-highlights" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Release Highlights" title="Direct link to Release Highlights" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="apache-hudi-1x">Apache Hudi 1.x<a href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release#apache-hudi-1x" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Apache Hudi 1.x" title="Direct link to Apache Hudi 1.x" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>XTable now builds against Apache Hudi 1.2.1, up from 0.14.0. The Hudi source and target support
Hudi table version 9, and the Hudi target builds the column stats index for existing Hudi tables.</p>
<p>A new module, <code>xtable-iceberg-pluggable-tf</code>, plugs into Hudi's pluggable table format. A Hudi writer
with this module on its classpath commits Iceberg metadata alongside every Hudi commit, so the
table stays readable as Iceberg without a separate sync.</p>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="secondary-index-for-any-source-table">Secondary index for any source table<a href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release#secondary-index-for-any-source-table" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Secondary index for any source table" title="Direct link to Secondary index for any source table" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>The Hudi target can now build a Hudi record index and secondary index over the files it registers.
This works for any source format that XTable reads, so an Iceberg or Delta table can get a
secondary index too. The sync job builds the index and keeps it up to date.</p>
<p>New Spark SQL extensions, shipped in <code>xtable-spark-runtime</code>, read that index. Once the extensions
are configured, point lookups on Iceberg tables in Spark use the index without any change to the
queries.</p>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="bug-fixes">Bug fixes<a href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release#bug-fixes" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Bug fixes" title="Direct link to Bug fixes" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>This release fixes several bugs in the Delta, Hudi and Parquet conversions. Some highlights:</p>
<ul>
<li class="">Delta tables with column mapping enabled now convert with correct partition values, instead of
null ones.</li>
<li class="">Delta data files outside the table base path keep their absolute paths.</li>
<li class="">A Hudi CLEAN that runs before an incremental sync no longer leaves deleted files in the target.</li>
<li class="">Parquet source files now report their record counts.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="packaging-and-licensing">Packaging and licensing<a href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release#packaging-and-licensing" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Packaging and licensing" title="Direct link to Packaging and licensing" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>The license issues listed as known issues in 0.4.0 are fixed. Every bundled jar now carries
complete license metadata for its shaded dependencies, and the build checks it. The
<code>xtable-utilities</code> bundled jar also shrank from 1.1 GB to 423 MB, and it now includes Iceberg's
<code>GlueCatalog</code> and <code>S3FileIO</code>.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="getting-the-release">Getting the release<a href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release#getting-the-release" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Getting the release" title="Direct link to Getting the release" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Download the source release, its signature and its checksum from the
<a class="" href="https://xtable.apache.org/releases/downloads">Downloads</a> page. Always verify the signature before you use the release.</p>
<p>The binary artifacts are on Maven Central under the <code>org.apache.xtable</code> group. For example, add the
Spark runtime jar as <code>org.apache.xtable:xtable-spark-runtime_2.12:0.5.0-incubating</code>.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_Vzrq" id="getting-involved">Getting involved<a href="https://xtable.apache.org/blog/apache-xtable-0.5.0-release#getting-involved" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Getting involved" title="Direct link to Getting involved" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Apache XTable™ (Incubating) grows through its contributors. We track work in
<a href="https://github.com/apache/incubator-xtable/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">GitHub issues</a> and we discuss it on the
<a href="mailto:dev@xtable.apache.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">dev mailing list</a>.</p>
<p>The easiest way to start is to:</p>
<ol>
<li class="">Try 0.5.0-incubating on your own tables and tell us how it goes.</li>
<li class="">Join the <a class="" href="https://xtable.apache.org/community/sync">community sync</a> and the dev mailing list.</li>
<li class="">Pick up a <a href="https://github.com/apache/incubator-xtable/contribute" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">good first issue</a>.</li>
</ol>]]></content>
